.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9597) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.55 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nFreelook camera speed in game embedding depends on time scale. The higher the time scale, the faster the camera moves and vice versa. While you can compensate for this manually by changing freelook speed, it can get tedious and is overall not expected behavior.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79d6625e-2715-47fc-8c38-99a21b34b7a5\n\nThis does not occur if the camera is overridden from the editor, as the editor's time scale is always `1.0` unless an editor plugin or CLI argument overrides it.\n\nI looked into fixing this in `View3DController::_update_freelook()`, but `Engine::get_singleton()->get_time_scale()` returns `1.0` because it's being queried in the editor instead of the running project. I assume there needs to be a way to communicate the game's time scale back to the editor to fix this.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Run any 3D project.\n- Increase or time scale in the game view.\n- Use the 3D mode to use freelook in game.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https